    fields:  # 23c0
      statement: "rust.yaml declares std::env::current_dir as fs_read. The same primitive is host_info_read in three other catalogues: python os.getcwd, go os.Getwd, c unistd.getcwd. rust-src env.rs:53 shows current_dir() is exactly os_imp::getcwd(), the getcwd(2) syscall returning process state, reading no file content. It also disagrees with its own module neighbours std::env::current_exe, temp_dir and home_dir, all host_info_read."  # 23c0
      root_cause: "Single-catalogue drift. The row was set without a cross-language parity check, and nothing enforces that one primitive carries one boundary across catalogues."  # 23c0
